cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use tcpcat in your research or tooling, please cite it."
title: "tcpcat: a fast network scanner with an eBPF/AF_XDP engine and sandboxed WASM detection scripting"
abstract: >-
  tcpcat is a network reconnaissance engine written in Go. It pairs a
  kernel-bypass (eBPF/AF_XDP) data path with service and OS detection, CVE
  correlation, sandboxed WebAssembly detection scripts, and JSON/SARIF
  reporting, for authorized security assessments.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Blondelle
    given-names: Nicolas
    alias: NycolazSec
repository-code: "https://github.com/NycolazSec/tcpcat"
url: "https://tcpcat.io"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 1.5.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
keywords:
  - network-scanner
  - ebpf
  - af-xdp
  - port-scanner
  - vulnerability-scanner
  - service-detection
  - webassembly
  - sarif
  - security
